# name: chained attribute access as RHS of assignment [ghi]
#

#--- Caspian -----------------------------------------------------------
$x = $foo.bar.gup
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- CaspJ -----------------------------------------------------------

#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#
# name: chained attribute access as RHS of assignment
#====================================================================


#====================================================================
# name: chained attribute assignment (single segment; identical to Section 6 case, re-anchored here) [ghi]
#

#--- Caspian -----------------------------------------------------------
$obj.name = 'alice'
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- CaspJ -----------------------------------------------------------

#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#
# name: chained attribute assignment (single segment; identical to Section 6 case, re-anchored here)
#====================================================================


#====================================================================
# name: chained attribute assignment (three segments) [ghi]
#

#--- Caspian -----------------------------------------------------------
$foo.bar.gup.baz = 'bear'
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- CaspJ -----------------------------------------------------------

#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#
# name: chained attribute assignment (three segments)
#====================================================================


#====================================================================
# name: chained attribute assignment (two segments, variable value) [ghi]
#

#--- Caspian -----------------------------------------------------------
$foo.bar.gup = $value
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- CaspJ -----------------------------------------------------------

#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#
# name: chained attribute assignment (two segments, variable value)
#====================================================================


# design decisions made unilaterally for Section 23:
#
#   - chained attribute access is left-associative: $foo.bar.gup is
#     [[{var:foo},bar],gup]. reads as "get bar off foo, then get gup off that."
#   - chained attribute assignment: the receiver of the setter is the chain
#     of everything up to and NOT including the last segment, applied
#     recursively; the setter's method name is the final segment plus "=".
#     e.g. $a.b.c.d = X → [[[{var:a},b],c], "d=", {args: [X]}]
#   - shape same as the single-segment case (Section 6) when there's only
#     one segment.
#
# method-call-inside-a-chain (get form) now handled by the multi-step chain
# walker in transpile_statement — `$foo.bar.gup(1)` walks left-to-right,
# wrapping each `.name` and `.name(args)` segment. See Section 23's
# "multi-line method chain" fixture for the shape. The assignment-to-
# chain-with-call form `$foo.bar.gup(1) = 2` is still unsupported — assigning
# to the return value of a method call has no obvious semantics.

